        "excerpt": "Learn when a home pregnancy test is most reliable, why testing early can give a false negative, and what to do after your result.",
        "faq": [
          {
            "answer": "Some sensitive tests may detect hCG before a missed period, but accuracy is lower that early. Check the product instructions and repeat the test after your period is due if the result is negative.",
            "question": "Can a pregnancy test be positive before a missed period?"
          },
          {
            "answer": "If you still suspect pregnancy, repeat the test after several days, when hCG may be easier to detect. Seek medical advice if another test is negative and your period still has not arrived.",
            "question": "When should I retest after a negative result?"
          },
          {
            "answer": "Not always. The NHS says tests can be taken at any time of day, but the FDA notes that first-morning urine may contain more hCG and can be helpful when testing very early. Follow your test's instructions.",
            "question": "Do I have to use first-morning urine?"
          }
        ],
