        "excerpt": "Mild cramps can happen throughout pregnancy. Learn about common causes, practical comfort measures and warning signs that need prompt medical care.",
        "faq": [
          {
            "answer": "Mild cramps can occur, but symptoms overlap with problems that need care. Contact a healthcare professional if cramps are persistent, worsening, one-sided or accompanied by bleeding, dizziness or shoulder pain.",
            "question": "Are period-like cramps normal in early pregnancy?"
          },
          {
            "answer": "Yes. Constipation and trapped wind are common causes of abdominal discomfort in pregnancy. Ask your clinician about safe diet, fluid, activity and treatment options if symptoms continue.",
            "question": "Can constipation cause cramps during pregnancy?"
          },
          {
            "answer": "Regular, increasingly frequent or painful tightenings can be a sign of labour. Before 37 weeks, regular cramps or tightenings require immediate contact with your maternity team because they may indicate preterm labour.",
            "question": "When could cramps mean labour?"
          }
        ],
        "featured": false,
        "heading": null,
