        "intro": "As labour approaches, the cervix changes from firm, long and closed to softer, thinner and open. Dilation describes opening in centimetres; effacement describes thinning and shortening, often recorded as a percentage. These findings help your care team understand what your cervix is doing, but they are not a countdown clock. People can remain slightly dilated for days or change quickly during labour.",
