        "excerpt": "Healthy pregnancy weight-gain ranges by pre-pregnancy BMI, how the pattern changes by trimester and when to discuss rapid or limited gain.",
        "faq": [
          {
            "answer": "Many people gain about 0.5–2 kg (1–5 lb) or none. Your pre-pregnancy BMI, symptoms and baby’s growth matter more than a single number.",
            "question": "How much weight should I gain in the first trimester?"
          },
          {
            "answer": "No. Multiple pregnancies use different, generally higher ranges. Ask your maternity team for an individual target.",
            "question": "Is the same range right for twins?"
          },
          {
            "answer": "Do not start a restrictive weight-loss plan without specialist advice. Focus on nutrition, safe activity and fetal growth with your clinician.",
            "question": "Should I lose weight while pregnant if my BMI is high?"
          }
        ],
