        "excerpt": "Compare practice contractions with labour contractions and learn which patterns and warning signs mean it is time to call your maternity unit.",
        "faq": [
          {
            "answer": "They are often painless but can be uncomfortable or occasionally strong. A pattern that intensifies, or any concern, should be discussed with your maternity team.",
            "question": "Can Braxton Hicks be painful?"
          },
          {
            "answer": "Labour contractions generally continue and progress despite rest or changing position. Braxton Hicks are more likely to ease, but this is not a definitive test.",
            "question": "Do real contractions stop when you rest?"
          },
          {
            "answer": "Start when tightenings feel regular or different from usual. Record several and call according to your maternity unit’s personal guidance.",
            "question": "When should I start timing contractions?"
          }
        ],
