        "excerpt": "A clear guide to normal pregnancy discharge, common colour changes, possible infection and how to recognise bleeding or leaking waters.",
        "faq": [
          {
            "answer": "Yes, thin clear or milky discharge without an unpleasant smell, pain or itching is usually normal and often increases during pregnancy.",
            "question": "Is milky white discharge normal?"
          },
          {
            "answer": "Yellow, green or grey discharge, strong odour, itching or pain can suggest infection, but a clinician should test rather than diagnose by colour alone.",
            "question": "What colour discharge means infection?"
          },
          {
            "answer": "Amniotic fluid is typically watery and may keep trickling uncontrollably. If unsure, use a pad and call your maternity unit for assessment.",
            "question": "How can I tell discharge from waters?"
          }
        ],
